{"name":"Nivea Creme blue tin","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Nivea Creme is a thick water-in-oil moisturiser sold in a blue tin with a white logo. People use it on dry skin of the face, hands and body to keep skin soft and smooth-looking.","It launched in 1911 and the tin dates from 1925, and it is reported as a long-lived household staple."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Applied to skin, for example after a shower, as one forum user described using Nivea on dry patches of arms and shoulders in winter.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Contains lanolin-derived emulsifier, so people with sensitivity to lanolin may react. Product details differ by market."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Nivea_Creme_BW_2025-07-05_16-51-45_s.jpg/960px-Nivea_Creme_BW_2025-07-05_16-51-45_s.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/Nivea_Creme_BW_2025-07-05_16-51-45_s.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Nivea Creme BW 2025-07-05 16-51-45 s","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Berthold Werner","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nivea_Creme_BW_2025-07-05_16-51-45_s.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Nivea_Creme.webp?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Nivea_Creme.webp?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Nivea Creme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Susana22BN","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nivea_Creme.webp","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Nivea_Ultra_Creme%2C_old_Swedish_tin_jar_2.jpg/960px-Nivea_Ultra_C